{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then encode the exploration and obstacle-recovery policy in compact specification automata. The policy gives strong preference to forward progress in clear space, uses short directed turns for side/front obstacles, allows a rare brief backward escape only after front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front-blocked recovery failure.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation into plant automata and place the task policy in specifications.",
    "Use one-shot action states in the specification so uncontrollable events are total, path_clear usually self-loops in commit states, and obstacle events force safe recovery.",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, use random_walk only as a secondary exploration action, use move_backward only in dedicated front recovery, and allow full_rotate only from a dedicated last-resort state."
  ],
